# scripts/check-generated-writers.ts reads the four generated-file markers, derives the writer each names, and warns
# when that writer cannot be found or when a file a writer declares it writes carries no marker.
# Each Scenario names the test that executes it.
Feature: A generated file names a writer the checkout can find

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::markerOf:_the_four_markers::a_top-level__generated,_in_any_position
  Scenario: A top-level _generated key is a marker
    # Gap: only one key position (after $schema) is checked, not "any position"
    Given a JSON file whose top-level keys are "$schema" then "_generated" naming "scripts/gen.ts — do not hand-edit"
    When its marker is read
    Then it is a "_generated" marker carrying that text

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::markerOf:_the_four_markers::a_$schema_the_registry_flags_generated
  Scenario: A $schema the registry flags as generated is a marker
    Given a JSON file whose $schema is "folio-library-index/v1", which the registry flags generated
    When its marker is read
    Then it is a "registry" marker

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::markerOf:_the_four_markers::generated:_front_matter
  Scenario: A generated front matter field is a marker
    Given a markdown file whose front matter has "generated: scripts/gen-docs-pages.ts — do not hand-edit"
    When its marker is read
    Then it is a "front-matter" marker

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::markerOf:_the_four_markers::an_HTML_banner
  Scenario: A leading HTML banner is a marker
    Given a markdown file opening with "<!-- Generated by scripts/prov-qaqc.ts. Do not hand-edit. -->"
    When its marker is read
    Then it is an "html-banner" marker

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::markerOf:_the_four_markers::a_file_that_only_MENTIONS_generation_deeper_in_is_not_marked
  Scenario: A file that only mentions generation deeper in is not marked
    Given a JSON file with "_generated" nested under "fields"
    And a markdown page saying "This page is not generated."
    When their markers are read
    Then neither has a marker

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::writersNamed::script_paths_and_bun_run_cat_tasks
  Scenario: Script paths and bun run cat tasks are read as writers
    Given marker text naming "folio-assistant-core/scripts/glossary-page.ts" and "bun run cat glossary:page"
    When the writers it names are read
    Then the paths are "folio-assistant-core/scripts/glossary-page.ts"
    And the tasks are "glossary:page"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::judge:_a_writer_is_real_when_the_checkout_can_find_it::a_path_found_from_an_instance_root,_or_a_known_task,_passes
  Scenario: A writer path found from an instance root, a known task, or a registry marker passes
    Given a checkout with "tools/scripts/gen.ts", instance roots "tools" and "content", and the known task "docs:pages"
    When a page marked with "scripts/gen.ts", with "bun run cat docs:pages", or by the registry is judged
    Then none of them is a warning

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::judge:_a_writer_is_real_when_the_checkout_can_find_it::a_writer_that_moved_away_is_a_warning_naming_it
  Scenario: A writer that is not in the checkout is a warning naming it
    Given a page whose banner names "content/scripts/gen.ts", which does not exist
    When it is judged
    Then the warning says the checkout does not have "content/scripts/gen.ts"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::judge:_a_writer_is_real_when_the_checkout_can_find_it::a_marker_naming_no_writer_is_a_warning
  Scenario: A marker naming no writer is a warning
    Given a page whose _generated marker says only "do not hand-edit"
    When it is judged
    Then the warning says it "names no writer"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::unmarkedWrites:_a_writer's_declared_files_must_carry_a_marker_(cat-harness#693)::an_unmarked_file_a_glob_matches_is_a_warning;_a_marked_one_is_not
  Scenario: An unmarked file a writer's glob matches is a warning
    Given "content/docs/marked.md" with generated front matter and "content/docs/bare.md" without
    And the task "docs:gen" declaring it writes "content:docs/*.md"
    When the unmarked writes are listed
    Then only "content/docs/bare.md" is reported
    And the problem says it is written by "docs:gen" but has no generated marker

  @test:scripts/tests/check-generated-writers.test.ts::unmarkedWrites:_a_writer's_declared_files_must_carry_a_marker_(cat-harness#693)::a_glob_matching_nothing,_or_naming_an_absent_instance,_is_reported
  Scenario: A glob that matches nothing or names an absent instance is reported
    Given a write declaration with the glob "gone/*.md"
    Then its problem says the glob matches no file
    And a declaration with the glob "elsewhere:x.md" is reported as not in this checkout
